Task:
# Task: Reject Pathological Content-Length Values

The HTTP parser currently accepts extremely large `Content-Length` header
values and attempts to parse the whole decimal string as an integer.

This can make a crafted response with a very long `Content-Length` value take a
long time to process on Python versions that do not protect `int()` conversion
with a digit limit. Newer Python versions may also expose the problem as a raw
`ValueError` instead of the protocol-level error expected by users of the
library.

Update the header handling so that a response with an unreasonably large
`Content-Length` value is rejected promptly as an `h11.ProtocolError`. Normal
valid `Content-Length` values and existing header behavior should continue to
work as before.

Do not change the public API of the `h11` package.


