Plan:
Modify h11/_headers.py to reject Content-Length values with an excessive number of digits. Add a module-level constant MAX_CONTENT_LENGTH_DIGITS = 20 (or similar). In normalize_and_validate, after the existing _content_length_re validation, check if len(value) > MAX_CONTENT_LENGTH_DIGITS and raise LocalProtocolError('Content-Length too large'). This will cause the existing header-parsing machinery to surface the error as a RemoteProtocolError (a subclass of h11.ProtocolError) for incoming responses, while leaving all valid values and other header behavior unchanged. Optionally, also wrap the int() conversion in h11/_connection.py's _body_framing with a try/except ValueError that raises RemoteProtocolError, as a defensive measure, but the primary fix is in _headers.py. No public API changes. Verify by running python -m pytest h11.

