Task:
# Task: Preserve Fragment Detection in _urlsplit Early Exit

The internal `_urlsplit()` helper can stop scanning a URL too early when the URL
contains a bracketed IPv6 host, a query string, and a fragment.

In this case the `#` fragment delimiter can be missed, causing the fragment to
be folded into the query. This also affects public URL canonicalization because
the fragment is not removed correctly.

Fix `_urlsplit()` so its early-exit logic only stops after all delimiter
positions it depends on have actually been found. The behavior should match a
full scan for URLs with IPv6 netlocs, query strings, and fragments, without
regressing normal URL parsing behavior.

Do not change the public API of the `w3lib` package.


