Task:
# Task: Support strftime-style datetime formats in patterns

`parse` is the inverse of `str.format`: it extracts typed values from text using
a format string. Add support for strftime/strptime-style datetime format
specifications in a field's type, for example `{:%Y-%m-%d}`, converting the
matched text into the corresponding `date` / `datetime` / `time` object.

Examples:

    parse("a {:%Y-%m-%d} b", "a 1997-07-16 b")[0] == date(1997, 7, 16)
    parse("a {:%Y-%b-%d} b", "a 1997-Feb-16 b")[0] == date(1997, 2, 16)

A format that also includes time and/or timezone directives (e.g. `%H`, `%z`)
must produce the appropriate `datetime`, including `tzinfo` when a timezone
directive is present. Several such fields, and mixing them with other field
types in the same pattern, must work.

Existing format specifications and all other behavior must be unchanged. Do not
change the public API.


