Task:
# Task: Don't warn when autospec-ing a class that uses `@cachedmethod`

Creating a `unittest.mock` autospec of a class whose methods are decorated with
`@cachedmethod` currently emits warnings. The cause is that introspecting the
decorated method on the *class* (where there is no instance, i.e. the object is
`None`) is not handled.

Make it possible to build an autospec of such a class without emitting any
warnings:

    unittest.mock.create_autospec(SomeClass, instance=True)  # no warnings

where `SomeClass` has one or more `@cachedmethod`-decorated methods. Normal
`@cachedmethod` behavior on real instances (caching, key handling) must be
completely unchanged. Do not change the public API.


