[developer report]
Fixed numeric delta handling in both tick() factories in freezegun/api.py.

1. FrozenDateTimeFactory.tick (around line 520): changed the annotation from `Union[datetime.timedelta, int]` to `Union[datetime.timedelta, numbers.Real]`, and wrapped the delta in `float(delta)` before building `datetime.timedelta(seconds=...)`. This lets `fractions.Fraction` and any other `numbers.Real` be converted to a float second count that timedelta can consume, instead of blowing up inside the timedelta constructor. `datetime.timedelta` deltas still flow through unchanged.

2. StepTickTimeFactory.tick (around line 545): changed the annotation from `Union[datetime.timedelta, int, None]` to `Union[datetime.timedelta, numbers.Real, None]`, and when a `numbers.Real` is passed it is converted with `datetime.timedelta(seconds=float(delta))` before adding, so int/float/Fraction deltas no longer raise a bare-addition TypeError. The default (`None` -> step_width) and `datetime.timedelta` behavior are preserved, and `move_to` still works because it passes a timedelta.

Both methods still return the new frozen time. The type annotations now reflect the accepted numeric types (`numbers.Real`). Tests in tests/test_ticking.py exercise the numeric and timedelta cases for these factories.

